@startuml
!theme plain
title Payment link · Selling to someone without an account
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Manager" as MG
actor "Buyer without an account" as G
participant "Frontend" as F
participant "NestJS API" as A
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
queue "Redis / BullMQ" as Q
participant "Worker" as W
participant "Stripe" as S
participant "SMTP" as M

== Getting the link ==
MG -> F : Wants a link for a size
F -> A : POST /payment-links\nskuId
activate A
alt Not a manager
  A --> F : 403 Forbidden
else The SKU doesn't exist or its product is deactivated
  A --> F : 404 NotFound
else There's already an active link
  A --> F : 200 PaymentLink, the same one as always
else None active
  A -> S : Creates the Payment Link with shipping address collection
  note right of S #ffe0e0 : Without the address, the webhook can't fill\nthe destination columns, which are NOT NULL:\nthe customer is charged and the order never gets recorded
  S --> A : URL
  A -> DB : Stores the link
  A --> F : 201 PaymentLink
end
deactivate A
note over A : A link sells **one** SKU, **one** unit, and is reusable.\nChanging the price or hitting zero deactivates it; the replacement\nis created lazily, and that 201 instead of 200 is how the manager\nfinds out the one they were handing out has stopped working

MG -> G : Passes them the URL
G -> S : Pays and fills in their address
S -> A : POST /webhooks/stripe

activate A
A -> DB : INSERT into webhook_events (UNIQUE)
A -> Q : Queues the settlement
A --> S : 200
deactivate A

Q -> W : Delivers the job
activate W
alt A **free** unit remains
  W -> DB : Creates or reuses the GUEST user by their email
  W -> DB : Creates the paid order and decrements the stock
  W -> Q : Queues the email with the order link
else No free unit remains
  W -> S : refund
  note right of W #ffe0e0
    Free, not merely present: units held by a
    pending checkout don't count. A payment through a
    healthy link can still end up refunded because of this,
    and it's the deliberate trade-off: refunding is reversible,
    overselling to someone who already reserved is not.
  end note
end
deactivate W
W -> M : Sends the email

== Reading the order without an account ==
G -> F : Opens the link from the email
F -> A : GET /guest-orders/ID
activate A
alt The owner is still GUEST
  A --> F : 200 OrderDetail
  note right of A #ffe0e0 : Possessing the URL **is** the credential. That's why this\nscheme has no customer: the buyer's email\ncan't reach whoever holds the link
else The owner has since verified an account
  A --> F : 404 NotFound
  F -> G : Sign in to view it
  note right of A : GUEST never signs in again, so\na link can't come back to life. The order moves\ninto their authenticated history
end
deactivate A

@enduml
